        <h1>OFFICIAL RULEBOOK & ROLE LIST</h1>

        <pre style="white-space: pre-wrap; font-family: inherit;">
==================================================
SECTION 1: GAME RULES
==================================================

Overview

Murder at Town Square is a social deduction card game where players take on secret roles in a town filled with hidden criminals, investigators, and citizens. Players must use deduction, teamwork, and deception to discover who is responsible for the murders before it is too late.

Each player receives a secret role with a unique ability and goal. Some players work together, while others must hide their true identity.

Objective

Each faction has a different objective.

Town

Find and eliminate all threats to the town.

Mafia

Secretly eliminate the town and take control of Town Square.

Neutral Roles

Complete their own personal victory condition.

Setup
Choose one player to be the Moderator.
Select the roles that will be used.
Shuffle the role cards.
Give one role card to each player.
Players secretly look at their role.
The Moderator begins the first Night.
Game Flow

Each round follows this order:

Night Phase
Morning Announcement
Discussion Phase
Voting Phase
Trial Phase
Execution (if voted guilty)
New Night Phase
Night Phase

During the Night:

Players close their eyes.
The Moderator calls roles in order.
Active roles perform their abilities.
Players silently choose targets.
The Moderator resolves all actions.
Morning Announcement

The Moderator announces what happened during the Night.

If a player died:

Their role is revealed.
Their card is placed in the Graveyard.
Any allowed information is announced.
Discussion Phase

Players discuss what happened.

Players may:

Share information.
Accuse other players.
Defend themselves.
Lie about their role.

Players are encouraged to use strategy and deduction.

Voting Phase

Players may nominate someone they believe is guilty.

If enough players vote to put someone on trial, the Trial Phase begins.

Trial Phase

The accused player gets a chance to defend themselves.

After the defense:

Players vote Guilty or Innocent.
A Guilty majority results in execution.
An Innocent majority allows the player to survive.
Death Rules

When a player dies:

Their role is revealed.
They may no longer vote.
They may not use abilities unless their role allows it.
They must follow the game's dead player rules.
Winning

The game ends when a faction completes its objective.

The winning faction is determined by the victory conditions of the remaining players.

==================================================
Town Roles

Town players work together to find and eliminate all threats. Town wins when all Mafia, Coven, and other enemies of the Town are eliminated.

Citizen

Faction: Town
Role Type: None

Night Ability
The Citizen has no Night ability.
The Citizen sleeps every Night.
Day Ability
May discuss, accuse players, and vote during trials.
Passive Abilities
None.
Goal

Help the Town eliminate all enemies.

Investigator

Faction: Town
Role Type: Investigative

Night Ability
Each Night, choose one living player to investigate.
The Investigator learns that player's exact role.
Uses
The Investigator has 2 investigations for the entire game.
After using both investigations, the Investigator has no more Night actions.
Day Ability
May share investigation results with the Town.
May keep information secret.
Passive Abilities
Investigation results are always accurate.
The Investigator does not learn if a player changed their appearance through disguises unless the rules specifically allow it.
Goal

Find dangerous roles and help the Town remove them.

Sheriff

Faction: Town
Role Type: Investigative

Night Ability
Each Night, choose one living player to investigate.
The Sheriff learns that player's alignment.

The result will be one of three:

Good

The player is working with the Town.

Bad

The player is a threat to the Town, such as Mafia or Coven.

Neutral

The player has their own win condition and is not part of the Town or a normal enemy faction.
Day Ability
May reveal investigation results.
May accuse players based on evidence.
Passive Abilities
The Sheriff does not learn a player's exact role.
The Sheriff only learns their alignment.
Goal

Find Bad players and protect the Town.

Doctor

Faction: Town
Role Type: Protective

Night Ability
Each Night, choose one living player to heal.
If that player would be killed during the Night, the death is prevented.
Day Ability
May discuss and vote normally.
Passive Abilities
The Doctor does not know if their heal worked.
The Doctor cannot revive dead players.
Goal

Keep Town members alive until all enemies are eliminated.

Bodyguard

Faction: Town
Role Type: Protective

Night Ability
Each Night, choose one living player to guard.

If that player is attacked:

The Bodyguard fights the attacker.
The attacker is eliminated.
The Bodyguard is also eliminated.
Day Ability
May discuss and vote normally.
Passive Abilities
The Bodyguard protects only the chosen player.
The Bodyguard does not know who attacked their target.
Goal

Protect important Town members.

Vigilante

Faction: Town
Role Type: Killing

Night Ability
Each Night, the Vigilante may choose one player to shoot.
The chosen player is eliminated if the attack succeeds.
Uses
The Vigilante has a limited number of bullets.
Day Ability
May discuss and vote normally.
Passive Abilities
The Vigilante can accidentally eliminate Town members.
The Vigilante must choose targets carefully.
Goal

Eliminate threats to the Town.

Veteran

Faction: Town
Role Type: Killing / Defensive

Night Ability
The Veteran may choose to go on Alert.
While on Alert, anyone who visits the Veteran is eliminated.
Uses
The Veteran has a limited number of Alerts.
Day Ability
May discuss and vote normally.
Passive Abilities
The Veteran cannot be safely visited while on Alert.
The Veteran does not choose who gets attacked.
Goal

Protect the Town by eliminating attackers.

Mayor

Faction: Town
Role Type: Leadership

Night Ability
The Mayor has no Night ability.
Day Ability
The Mayor may reveal themselves during the Day.
After revealing, their vote becomes stronger.
Passive Abilities
Once revealed, everyone knows the Mayor's identity.
The Mayor becomes a major voting power for the Town.
Goal

Lead the Town to victory.

Medium

Faction: Town
Role Type: Information

Night Ability
The Medium may communicate with eliminated players.
Dead players may provide information to the Medium.
Day Ability
May share information learned from dead players.
Passive Abilities
The Medium cannot bring dead players back.
The Medium cannot force dead players to tell the truth.
Goal

Use information from eliminated players to help the Town.

Tracker

Faction: Town
Role Type: Investigative

Night Ability
Choose one player.
Learn who that player visited during the Night.
Day Ability
May share tracking information.
Passive Abilities
The Tracker sees movement, not exact actions.
Goal

Find suspicious activity and identify enemies.

Lookout

Faction: Town
Role Type: Investigative

Night Ability
Choose one player.
Learn who visited that player during the Night.
Day Ability
May reveal visitor information.
Passive Abilities
The Lookout does not know what visitors did.
Only learns who visited.
Goal

Discover criminals through their actions.

Psychic

Faction: Town
Role Type: Investigative

Night Ability
Receives information about possible players involved in evil actions.
Day Ability
May share visions with the Town.
Passive Abilities
Information may not identify the exact enemy.
Goal

Help the Town discover hidden threats.

Transporter

Faction: Town
Role Type: Support

Night Ability
Choose two players.
Swap their positions.

Example:

Player A is attacked.
Player B was transported with Player A.
The attack affects Player B instead.
Day Ability
May discuss and vote normally.
Passive Abilities
The Transporter does not know what actions are redirected.
Goal

Protect allies and confuse enemies.

Jailor

Faction: Town
Role Type: Control / Killing

Night Ability
During the Day, choose one player to jail.
At Night, the jailed player cannot act.
The Jailor may choose to execute the jailed player.
Uses
Limited executions.
Day Ability
Selects who will be jailed.
Passive Abilities
A jailed player cannot use Night abilities.
The Jailor controls the jail conversation.
Goal

Remove threats while protecting the Town.
Mafia Roles

The Mafia is a secret criminal organization working together to eliminate the Town and other enemies. Mafia members know each other and coordinate their actions at Night.

The Mafia wins when they control the Town Square by eliminating enough opposing players.

Mafia Member

Faction: Mafia
Role Type: Killing / Basic Mafia

Night Ability
Each Night, the Mafia chooses one living player to attack.
The chosen player is eliminated unless protected or otherwise saved.
Day Ability
Pretend to be a normal Town member.
Discuss, accuse, and vote to mislead the Town.
Passive Abilities
Knows the identity of other Mafia members.
Works with the Mafia team.
Goal

Eliminate the Town and all opposing factions.

Godfather

Faction: Mafia
Role Type: Mafia Leader

Night Ability
Each Night, choose the Mafia's target to eliminate.
If the Godfather does not choose a target, another Mafia member may perform the attack.
Day Ability
Lead discussions and manipulate votes.
Passive Abilities
Appears Good to the Sheriff.
Leads the Mafia.
Cannot be easily identified by investigations.
Goal

Lead the Mafia to victory.

Mafioso

Faction: Mafia
Role Type: Mafia Killer

Night Ability
Performs the Mafia's attack when ordered.
If the Godfather is alive, follows the Godfather's orders.
If the Godfather dies, the Mafioso takes over the Mafia attack.
Day Ability
Pretends to be a Town member.
Passive Abilities
Becomes the new Godfather if the original Godfather dies.
Goal

Help the Mafia eliminate all enemies.

Blackmailer

Faction: Mafia
Role Type: Information / Control

Night Ability
Choose one player to blackmail.

The blackmailed player:

Cannot reveal information during the Day.
Cannot speak during trials.
Cannot tell the Town their role or results.
Day Ability
The blackmailed player must remain silent according to the rules.
Passive Abilities
Knows who they blackmailed.
Goal

Prevent the Town from sharing information.

Consigliere

Faction: Mafia
Role Type: Investigative

Night Ability
Choose one player to investigate.
Learn their exact role.
Uses
2 investigations per game.
Day Ability
Give useful information to the Mafia.
Help choose important targets.
Passive Abilities
Investigation results are accurate.
Goal

Find important roles and help the Mafia eliminate them.

Janitor

Faction: Mafia
Role Type: Deception

Night Ability
Choose one player to clean.

If that player dies:

Their role is hidden.
The Town does not learn what role they had.
Uses
Limited number of cleans.
Day Ability
Pretend to be innocent.
Passive Abilities
Helps hide Mafia kills.
Goal

Keep the Town from learning important information.

Framer

Faction: Mafia
Role Type: Deception

Night Ability
Choose one player to frame.

The framed player appears suspicious to investigations.

Day Ability
Accuse framed players to make them look guilty.
Passive Abilities
The effect lasts according to the game's investigation rules.
Goal

Make innocent players appear guilty.

Disguiser

Faction: Mafia
Role Type: Deception

Night Ability
Choose another player.
The Disguiser changes their appearance to match that player.
Day Ability
Pretend to be another role.
Passive Abilities
Investigations may see the disguised identity instead of the real role.
Goal

Hide the Mafia's identities.

Forger

Faction: Mafia
Role Type: Deception

Night Ability
Choose a player.
Create a fake Last Will for them.

If that player dies:

The fake information is shown instead of their real message.
Uses
Limited number of forgeries.
Day Ability
Use fake information to confuse the Town.
Passive Abilities
Can only affect players before they die.
Goal

Spread false information.

Ambusher

Faction: Mafia
Role Type: Killing / Defensive

Night Ability
Choose one player to ambush.

If another player visits that target:

The visitor is attacked.
Day Ability
Pretend to be innocent.
Passive Abilities
Protects Mafia targets by removing visitors.
Goal

Eliminate important Town roles.

Hypnotist

Faction: Mafia
Role Type: Deception

Night Ability
Choose a player to hypnotize.
Give them a fake message or false information.

Examples:

"You were attacked."
"You were healed."
"You saw someone visit."
Day Ability
The hypnotized player may unknowingly share false information.
Passive Abilities
Creates confusion without directly attacking.
Goal

Mislead the Town.

Consort

Faction: Mafia
Role Type: Support / Role Blocking

Night Ability
Choose one player to distract.

The target:

Cannot use their Night ability.
Day Ability
Pretend to be a harmless role.
Passive Abilities
Stops important Town roles from acting.
Goal

Prevent the Town from using powerful abilities.
Neutral Roles

Neutral roles do not belong to the Town, Mafia, or Coven. They have their own personal goals and may help or hurt other factions depending on what benefits them.

Survivor

Faction: Neutral
Role Type: Survival

Night Ability
Each Night, the Survivor may use a Vest.
A Vest protects the Survivor from being eliminated that Night.
Uses
Limited number of Vests.
Day Ability
May discuss, accuse, and vote like any other player.
Passive Abilities
The Survivor has no team.
Other players may choose to help or eliminate the Survivor.
Goal

Survive until the end of the game.

Jester

Faction: Neutral
Role Type: Trickster

Night Ability
The Jester has no Night ability.
Day Ability
Attempts to convince the Town that they are suspicious.
May lie about their role or actions.
Passive Abilities
Does not win by surviving.
Must be eliminated by the Town.
Goal

Be voted guilty and executed by the Town.

Executioner

Faction: Neutral
Role Type: Manipulation

Night Ability
Has no active Night ability.
Setup Ability
At the beginning of the game, the Executioner receives a target.
Their target is a living player.
Day Ability
Must convince the Town to execute their target.
Passive Abilities
The Executioner loses their original goal if their target dies another way.
Goal

Get your assigned target executed by the Town.

Serial Killer

Faction: Neutral Evil
Role Type: Killing

Night Ability
Each Night, choose one player to attack.
That player is eliminated unless protected.
Day Ability
Pretend to be innocent.
Avoid being discovered.
Passive Abilities
Works alone.
Does not know Mafia or Coven plans.
Goal

Be the last player alive.

Arsonist

Faction: Neutral Evil
Role Type: Killing

Night Ability

The Arsonist has two actions:

Douse

Choose one player.
That player is covered in gasoline.

Ignite

Burn all players currently doused.
All doused players are eliminated.
Day Ability
Pretend to be innocent.
Passive Abilities
Can wait and attack multiple players at once.
Goal

Eliminate everyone else and survive.

Werewolf

Faction: Neutral Evil
Role Type: Killing

Night Ability

On normal Nights:

The Werewolf does not attack.

On Full Moon Nights:

Transform into a Werewolf.
Attack a chosen player.
Attack anyone who visits the target.
Day Ability
Pretend to be innocent.
Passive Abilities
Becomes stronger during Full Moon Nights.
Harder to stop while transformed.
Goal

Eliminate all other players.

Witch

Faction: Neutral
Role Type: Control

Night Ability
Choose one player.
Choose another player as their target.
Force the first player to use their ability on the second player.

Example:

The Witch controls a Vigilante.
The Witch forces the Vigilante to shoot someone.
Day Ability
Pretend to be innocent.
Passive Abilities
Can control powerful roles against their own team.
Goal

Survive and complete the Witch's victory condition.

Amnesiac

Faction: Neutral
Role Type: Role Changing

Night Ability
Choose a dead player's role.
Remember that role.

After remembering:

The Amnesiac becomes that role.
Gains that role's abilities and goal.
Day Ability
May hide their future plans.
Passive Abilities
Cannot remember a role that is not available.
Goal

Complete the goal of the role they remember.

Vampire

Faction: Vampire
Role Type: Conversion

Night Ability
Choose one player to bite.
That player becomes a Vampire.
Rules
Vampires work together.
Converted players join the Vampire team.
Day Ability
Pretend to be other roles.
Passive Abilities
Vampires know their teammates.
Goal

Convert players and eliminate opposing factions.

Guardian Angel

Faction: Neutral
Role Type: Protection

Setup Ability
At the beginning of the game, the Guardian Angel receives a target.
Night Ability
Protect the target from attacks.
Day Ability
Defend your target during discussion.
Passive Abilities
If your target survives, you succeed.
Goal

Keep your assigned player alive.

Pirate

Faction: Neutral
Role Type: Duelist

Night Ability
Challenge one player to a duel.
Both players secretly choose a move.
The winner survives.
Day Ability
Pretend to be innocent.
Passive Abilities
Works alone.
Goal

Win enough duels to complete the Pirate's objective.

Plaguebearer

Faction: Neutral Evil
Role Type: Infection

Night Ability
Infect one player each Night.
Passive Abilities
Infected players spread the plague.
Transformation

When all living players are infected:

The Plaguebearer becomes Pestilence.
Goal

Spread the plague and become powerful enough to win.

Pestilence

Faction: Neutral Evil
Role Type: Killing

Night Ability
Attack one player each Night.
Passive Abilities
Immune to most attacks.
Extremely difficult to eliminate.
Day Ability
Pretend to be innocent.
Goal

Be the last player alive.

Juggernaut

Faction: Neutral Evil
Role Type: Killing

Night Ability
Attack one player each Night.
Passive Abilities
Gains stronger abilities after each kill.

Examples:

Stronger attacks.
Better defenses.
Goal

Eliminate everyone else.
Coven Roles (Expansion)

The Coven is a powerful evil faction that works together to eliminate the Town, Mafia, and other opposing factions.

Coven members know each other and coordinate their actions during the Night.
Potion Master
Coven Leader

Faction: Coven
Role Type: Leadership / Information Control

Night Ability

Each Night, choose one living player to Redact.

A Redacted player's role information becomes hidden.

Effects of Redaction:

Investigator

If the Investigator investigates a Redacted player, they receive:

Role: REDACTED

The Investigator knows the information was blocked but does not learn the player's real role.

Sheriff

If the Sheriff investigates a Redacted player, they receive:

Alignment: REDACTED

The Sheriff cannot see if the player is Good, Bad, or Neutral.

Other Information Roles

Any ability that would reveal the player's identity or faction receives a Redacted result.

Faction: Coven
Role Type: Support

Night Ability

Each Night, use one random potion on chosen player.

The Potion Master has three potions:

Heal Potion
Protects a player from being eliminated that Night.
Attack Potion
Attacks and eliminates one player.
Reveal Potion
Learns a player's exact role.
Day Ability
Share or hide information to help the Coven.
Passive Abilities
Each potion has limited uses.
Goal

Use potions strategically to help the Coven win.

Necromancer

Faction: Coven
Role Type: Role Copy / Support

Night Ability
Choose a dead player's role.
Use that role's Night ability.

Examples:

Use a dead Doctor's heal.
Use a dead Vigilante's shot.
Rules
The dead player does not return.
The Necromancer only copies the ability.
Day Ability
Pretend to be another role.
Passive Abilities
Can use dead players as resources.
Goal

Use fallen players to help the Coven.

Poisoner

Faction: Coven
Role Type: Killing

Night Ability
Choose one player to poison.
Poison Rules
The poison does not kill immediately.
The poisoned player dies later unless saved by a healing ability.
Day Ability
Pretend to be innocent.
Passive Abilities
Poison can bypass some defenses.
Goal

Secretly eliminate enemies.

Medusa

Faction: Coven
Role Type: Killing / Deception

Night Ability
Choose to use Stone Gaze.

If another player visits the Medusa:

The visitor is turned to stone.
The visitor is eliminated.
Additional Ability
Can hide the roles of players eliminated by Stone Gaze.
Day Ability
Pretend to be a harmless role.
Passive Abilities
Punishes players who investigate or visit.
Goal

Eliminate enemies of the Coven.

Coven Member

Faction: Coven
Role Type: Basic Coven

Night Ability
Assists the Coven's plans.
Performs actions assigned by the Coven.
Day Ability
Pretend to be a Town member.
Vote and discuss to mislead others.
Passive Abilities
Knows other Coven members.
Goal

Help the Coven eliminate all opposing factions.
==================================================

# Murder at Town Square

# Role Selection Manual

## Creating a Balanced Game

A balanced game should give every faction a realistic chance to win.

When choosing roles, the Moderator should consider:

* Number of players
* Number of killing roles
* Amount of information roles
* Amount of protection roles
* Number of evil players
* Number of neutral players

A game should never have:

* Too many killing roles
* Too many investigation roles
* Too many protection roles
* Too many neutral roles with separate win conditions

---

# Recommended Faction Balance

For most games:

## Town

About **60% of players**

Town should have:

* Information roles
* Protective roles
* A few special abilities
* Citizens to create uncertainty

## Mafia / Coven

About **25% of players**

Evil factions should have:

* A killing ability
* Information control
* Support abilities

## Neutral Roles

About **15% of players**

Neutral roles should add chaos without overwhelming the game.

---

# Player Count Role Guides

## 5 Players

### Factions:

* 3 Town
* 1 Mafia
* 1 Neutral

### Example:

Town:

* Sheriff
* Doctor
* Citizen

Mafia:

* Mafioso

Neutral:

* Survivor

---

# 6 Players

### Factions:

